ties plans spending up 12%, with a C$450M tender in Q2.\n- Pellham is the largest single buyer of grid equipment in Caldria.\n- VLTX won 60% of the last tender round.\n- VLTX utility order intake has risen each quarter: C$610M in 2025Q4, then 640, 655 and 670 in 2026Q3.\n\n**Data centres (growing more slowly)**\n- Grid connection requests are expected to grow 9% in 2027, which is slower than in 2026. Power availability is limiting new sites.\n- The connection queue grew 4% in Q3 2026. Data centres make up 60% of new requests, and the average wait is 26 months. That is a backlog of demand, but the wait shows a constraint on how fast it turns into orders.\n\n**Risks**\n- Pellham withdrew a planned C$2.4B equity offering after investor demand fell short. It is on negative watch at Caldria Ratings, and utility bond spreads widened 30bp to 165bp in Q3. Pellham's plan, and so the Q1 tender, could slip or shrink if funding stays tight. Norvane looks better placed. My colleagues' funding work is in n3.r1, n5.r1 and n6.r1.\n\n**What I couldn't check**\n- I couldn't find the VLTX customer mix, so I don't know how much of VLTX's orders depend on Pellham.\n- I also couldn't find how much of the capital plans is equipment spending.","ttft_ms":1675,"type":"result","duration_ms":68061,"uuid":"47090978-f6db-40f8-8efb-bcb962319b9a","ttft_stream_ms":1081,"time_to_request_ms":187,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":7,"system_prompt":18,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":10,"input_attachments":35,"input_hooks":6,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":16,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":48,"init_frame_send":2,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":13,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":4,"request_announcements":11,"query_setup":0,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":3,"message_normalization":3,"client_creation":2,"request_build":5},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":65,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":84,"time_to_request_ma